`update`: 290k of json files was giving this OOM, moving into single JSONL file and then read it by Duckdb was successful. (something is going wrong with reading a lot of json files)

I had a very similar problem with `duckdb`, and found some references to problems with `jemalloc` in systems with `transparent hugepages` enabled. I wrote a small C program that switches off `transparent hugepages` for the current process (and processest started by it), and that has solved the problem for me, at least.

The entire wrapper program looks like this:

```
#include <stdio.h>

#include <unistd.h>
#include <sys/prctl.h>

int main(int argc, char **argv)
{
  int res;
  res = prctl(PR_SET_THP_DISABLE, 1, 0, 0, 0);
  execvp(*(argv+1), argv+1);
}
```

The crucial part is `prctl(PR_SET_THP_DISABLE, 1, 0, 0, 0);`.

